# ManhwaManiacs (OVH VPS) — pull the newest CI-built iOS .ipa so SideStore can
# offer it as an over-the-air update. Closes the loop from `git push github` to
# an Update badge on the phone.
#
# This is the VPS counterpart of ops/manhwamaniacs-ios-sync.cron (which targeted
# the NAS paths). Only the branch and destination differ; the script itself is
# shared — ops/ios-sync-cron.sh -> ops/fetch-ios-build.sh.
#
# Install (on the VPS, as root):
#   sudo install -m 644 /srv/manhwamaniacs/app/ops/vps/manhwamaniacs-ios-sync.cron \
#        /etc/cron.d/manhwamaniacs-ios-sync
# (the installed filename must not contain a dot, or cron ignores it)
#
# Runs as root so it can chown the published .ipa to uid 1000, which is what the
# backend container reads it as (see the ./ipa mount in ops/vps/docker-compose.yml).
#
# Credentials: none needed while the GitHub repo is public — release assets are
# anonymously downloadable. If the repo is private, the script falls back to the
# Actions artifact API, which needs a token with Actions:read at /root/.gh_token.
#
# Every 10 minutes; an iOS build takes ~5 min, so a push shows up on the phone
# within roughly a quarter hour. A run with nothing new costs one API call.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MM_IOS_BRANCH=feat/vps-slim-source-native

*/10 * * * * root /srv/manhwamaniacs/app/ops/ios-sync-cron.sh /srv/manhwamaniacs/ipa
